
This plugin receives packages with type "kdeconnect.sftp" and reads the
following fields:

  ip (string): ip of the currently active network on device
  port (string): port where sftp server starts
  user (string): username to connect to sftp server
  password (string): one session password to access sftp server
  path (string): root directory to access device filesystem

This plugin sends packages with type "kdeconnect.sftp" and fills the
following fields:

  startBrowsing (boolean): tell device to start sftp server and notify desktop


Platform notes
==============

On Linux the remote filesystem is mounted with sshfs and added to Dolphin's
Places.

On Windows the remote filesystem is mounted to a drive letter (e.g. Z:) using
SSHFS-Win (https://github.com/winfsp/sshfs-win), which in turn requires WinFsp
(https://winfsp.dev). The mount is driven by sshfs.exe, located on the PATH.

  * Runtime requirement: install SSHFS-Win (which bundles WinFsp).
  * The plugin mounts automatically when a paired device becomes reachable and
    unmounts (releasing the drive letter) when it disconnects.
  * The "Browse" action opens File Explorer at the drive letter.
  * A free drive letter is claimed automatically, scanning from Z: down to D:.
  * If sshfs.exe cannot be found, the mount fails with a user-facing error.

